meta {
  name: Search
  type: http
  seq: 21
}

get {
  url: {{api}}/bonds/{{bondId}}/search?q=walk
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  q: walk
  ~limit: 20
  ~cursor: {{nextCursor}}
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.status === 200 && res.body.nextCursor) bru.setVar("nextCursor", res.body.nextCursor);
}

docs {
  The archive, found by words: the days on which one entry you can read holds every word of q, newest first, each day whole. Case and accents do not matter (cafe finds Café); whole words only. Your own entry is found before it is revealed; your partner's only once it has been.

  A blank q, or one longer than 100 characters, is 422 on q, which is never sent back. There is no count of matches; only a null nextCursor means the end.
}
